msgstr "Period tables understate the life expectancy of later cohorts, because medicine keeps improving. That is why there is a \"+2 years\" option (an assumption, in the Plan, off by default). The confidence interval of this result reflects only the sampling error of the market simulation, not the uncertainty of the tables."

