msgstr "In expert mode you can choose the textbook model (Brownian motion with geometric growth, no regimes and no fat tails). In that model the median final value is exactly equal to the CAGR you enter. In the realistic model the median is slightly higher, because the distribution is slightly left-skewed; the mean of the log returns is preserved exactly."

